## Standalone fences (base.md §15.1). `fence(order)` orders memory
## accesses without a location; `fence(.signal)` is a compiler-only barrier
## for signal handlers. The compiler lowers every call to the fence
## instruction itself; this declaration gives the call its name and the
## `Ordering` cases it accepts.

pub enum Ordering:
    relaxed
    acquire
    release
    acq_rel
    seq_cst
    signal

pub func fence(order: Ordering):
    return
